{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786429032,"nonce":"oxo72UwOu8DumQ92mntidzBRHqs=","message":"Decided from a real corpus and recorded as ADR 0026. Evidence: Alertmanager's own dispatch.DefaultRouteOpts, plus kube-prometheus-stack, kube-prometheus, OpenShift cluster-monitoring-operator and Grafana Alerting shipping configs (group_interval: 5m is the one value nobody overrides), and 155 rendered rules from kube-prometheus-stack 88.2.0 where for: 15m is both mode (69 rules, 44.5%) and median — 5m is only 12.9%. The repo's own capture at group_interval: 30s is kept as the counter-case.\n\nThe derivation found three defects, not one:\n1. refire_grace's clock starts at the upstream EndsAt, so a re-fire pays the rule's whole for: again INSIDE the window. 600s was reachable for 24% of the corpus and THE MODAL for: 15m RULE COULD NEVER REACH IT. -\u003e 1200s.\n2. group_close_delay (300s) was SHORTER than refire_grace (600s), so the generation closed halfway through the grace and the reopen posted a new root card anyway. oto's own tuning page stated the rule its own defaults broke. -\u003e 1200s.\n3. The flap formula was missing the transport floor: a cycle costs group_interval + max(group_interval, for), not for + group_interval. At group_interval 5m a 30-minute window holds at most 6 transitions FOR ANY RULE SHAPE, and 2 for the modal rule — so 5-in-30m WAS UNREACHABLE FOR EVERY RULE IN THE CORPUS. Dead code that looked configured. -\u003e window 7200s; threshold 5 survives (42% of the modal ceiling).\n\nWhich error oto prefers: THE LOUD ONE. Too short fragments threads and every fragment is a loud new root card; too long folds a genuine re-fire into a stale thread, which is the shape of a missed page. So 1200 is the SMALLEST value reaching the modal rule, not the largest covering every rule — covering the for: 1h tail would have meant a 65-minute grace merging separate incidents for the 76% that never needed it.\n\nBounds re-checked, none moved; the flap_window floor of 300s is kept precisely because the one real capture runs group_interval 30s.\n\nLeft open, a product decision: ADR 0020 grants refired a broadcast because its quiet form is invisible, but §H.6's verbosity table drops that reply entirely at firing_only/firing_and_resolved. On a quieter-than-default channel a re-fire inside the grace is SILENT, and a longer grace widens the hole. Pinned by refire_visibility_test.go.","files":null}]}